# Test: testing criteria (`y-tst-testing-criteria`)

Use this rule when a work item needs **Testing Criteria** that Tech and QA can use to judge pass/fail **without** prescribing specific test cases.

Product owners define **what must be true**; QA defines **how to test it** (see `.cursor/rules/y-rules/test/y-tst-test-cases.mdc`).

## When to use

- Behavior changes that need explicit pass/fail boundaries
- Domain-expert or PO review follow-ups
- Handoff from implementation to QA before release sign-off

Do **not** use this rule for E2E run reports. When generative-search rules are installed, use `.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc` (and conversation formatting via `.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-conversation.mdc`).

---

## AskQuestion gate (mandatory)

Before drafting content, use **`AskQuestion`** to choose the **output type**. Wait for the answer before writing.

| Option | File saved | Also show in chat |
|--------|------------|-------------------|
| **doc** | Full markdown doc (default structure) | Path to the saved file |
| **Slack** | Same full markdown doc as **doc** | Full paste-ready body for the Jira **Testing Criteria** custom field |
| **Jira** | Same full markdown doc as **doc** | Concise paste-ready body for the Jira **Testing Criteria** custom field |
| **other** | Same full markdown doc as **doc** (unless user opts out) | Format the user describes |

**Slack** and **Jira** both target the ticket’s **Testing Criteria** field — not Jira comments. **Slack** is the fuller field paste; **Jira** is a shorter, tighter field paste.

If the user already stated the type in the same message, still confirm via **`AskQuestion`** unless they explicitly said to skip.

Resolve **`<JIRA-KEY>`** from the ticket, branch name, or user input before generating output.

---

## Artifact location and filename (all types)

**Always** save the full markdown document for **doc**, **Slack**, **Jira**, and **other** (unless the user explicitly opts out of the file for **other**).

- Folder: **`docs/<JIRA-KEY>/`** (for example `docs/VAP-2291/`).
- Filename: **`testing-criteria-<jira-key>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>.md`**
  - **`<jira-key>`** — lowercase Jira key (for example `vap-2291`).
  - **`<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>`** — local date and time when the document is **written** (24-hour time, minute precision).
- Example: `docs/VAP-2291/testing-criteria-vap-2291-20260812-1006.md`
- One criteria file per write unless the user specifies a different path.
- Track the file in git when created for implementation work.

The saved file uses the **same full structure** as the **doc** type (H1, header block, Acceptance Criteria, Definition of Done). **Slack** and **Jira** types add a **second**, tailored excerpt in chat — they do **not** replace or shorten the file.

---

## Shared content rules (all types)

- Criteria only — **no** step-by-step test cases (see `y-tst-test-cases.mdc`).
- **B2 English:** clear, professional, short sentences.
- **Audience:** Tech and QA; avoid implementation file paths and code-level detail.
- Organize acceptance rules as numbered groups with **Pass / Fail** conditions (tables or bold **Pass:** / **Fail:** lines).
- Include **Definition of Done for Testing** (checklist mirroring criterion groups).
- When conversation wording matters, allow **semantic equivalence** in pass conditions — state that once in DoD, not in every row.

Do **not** include **Product Goal** or **Reference Implementation** sections in any output type.

