## Output by type

Every type **must** write the [canonical markdown file](#artifact-location-and-filename-all-types) first, then deliver the type-specific output below.

### doc — full document

Save the file using the [filename pattern](#artifact-location-and-filename-all-types) above. Tell the user the file path.

**H1 title:**

```markdown
# VAP-2291 - Testing Criteria - 20260812-1006
```

**Pattern:** `<JIRA-KEY> - Testing Criteria - <YYYYMMDD-HHMM>` (same timestamp as the filename).

**Header block** (required, immediately after H1):

```markdown
**Work item:** [<JIRA-KEY>](https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/<JIRA-KEY>)
**Audience:** Tech and QA
**Purpose:** <One sentence: what “done and correct” means for this change.>
```

**Body:** full [Required structure](#required-structure-doc) below — Title Case headings, horizontal rules sparingly.

---

### Slack — Jira Testing Criteria field (full paste)

**File:** save the same [canonical markdown file](#artifact-location-and-filename-all-types) as **doc** — do not skip or shorten it.

**Chat:** also provide a **full paste-ready excerpt** for the ticket’s **Testing Criteria** custom field (not a Jira comment).

**Do (chat excerpt):**

- Lead with acceptance criteria groups and Pass/Fail requirements.
- End with a compact **Definition of Done for Testing** checklist.
- Use scannable markdown (headings, tables, or bullets) that renders well in Jira.

**Do not (chat excerpt):**

- Mention the ticket key or ticket code anywhere in the body.
- Add Jira links, “Work item:”, audience lines, or purpose preamble.
- Repeat the ticket title or restate obvious context from the field location.
- Include test-case steps or implementation detail.

Omit metadata wrappers in the chat excerpt — the field already identifies the ticket.

---

### Jira — Jira Testing Criteria field (concise paste)

**File:** save the same [canonical markdown file](#artifact-location-and-filename-all-types) as **doc** — do not skip or shorten it.

**Chat:** also provide a **concise paste-ready excerpt** for the ticket’s **Testing Criteria** custom field (not a Jira comment).

**Do (chat excerpt):**

- Cover acceptance criteria and Definition of Done, but **shorter** than the **Slack** excerpt.
- Prefer tight bullets or a slim Pass/Fail table — highest-signal rules only.
- Keep sentences short; cut repetition and background the field does not need.

**Do not (chat excerpt):**

- Format as a Jira **comment** or thread message — this is **only** for the Testing Criteria field.
- Mention the ticket key or ticket code anywhere in the body.
- Add Jira links, “Work item:”, audience lines, or purpose preamble.
- Over-explain or duplicate the full **Slack** field paste when a lean summary is enough.
- Include test-case steps or implementation detail.

Omit metadata wrappers in the chat excerpt — the field already identifies the ticket.

